 "notes": "Where the list is: it starts on n94.jpg (printed p. 79, Nos. 115-132) and ends on n95.jpg (p. 80, Nos. 133-167). Running text follows it on p. 80 (\"It is satisfactory to note…\"), so n93.jpg (p. 78, the end of the previous section's prose) and n96.jpg have no part of it. I did not open n96.\n\nCounts check out: 53 stations (Nos. 115-167, no gaps or repeats), which matches \"fifty-three\". There are 39 asterisks, which matches \"thirty-nine\". By coast: Isle of Man 3 of 5, N.-W. England 4 of 4, North Wales 7 of 9, South Wales 6 of 6, Bristol Channel 6 of 8, South-Western England 13 of 21.\n\nLayout: the coast names are printed sideways beside braces. They read \"Isle of Man.\", \"N.-W. England.\", \"North Wales.\", \"South Wales.\", \"Bristol Channel.\" and \"South-Western England.\". I left out the final full stop in the coast field. Each number is printed with a full stop (\"*117.\"). I kept that stop in \"printed\" but not in \"number\". The type column is set in small capitals (L.H. / L.V.). Rows with a keeper have a comma and leader dots after the name. I wrote the leaders as a fixed \"........\" because their exact count means nothing. Rows without a keeper end with a full stop after the name. I left out each row's closing full stop from the name and keeper fields. Where a keeper's name runs onto a second line in the print, I joined it onto one line.\n\nKeepers: \"Daniel Kneale and George Cumming\" (Selker) and \"S. Work and J. Clague\" (River Dee) are each split into two people, since no \"Messrs\" joins them. Every \"Messrs …\" entry stays as one, as you asked. At Holyhead Breakwater the print is set tight (\"MessrsPrichard,Roberts,\"). I wrote it with normal spacing: \"Messrs Prichard, Roberts, and Hughes\".\n\nSpellings copied as printed, which may be period forms or misprints:\n- \"Chickens Rock\" has no apostrophe.\n- \"Air\" is Point of Air.\n- \"Caldy\" is Caldey.\n- \"Flatholm\" is Flat Holm.\n- \"Sevenstones\" is one word.\n- \"Prichard\" has no t.\n- \"Messrs Havells and Wynen\" at Scarweather: \"Havells\" may be a misprint for Howells, which appears one row above at Helwick.\n- \"Ebgar\" at Plymouth Breakwater may be a misprint for Edgar.\n\nThe OCR's \"Portland Bull\" is wrong. The image clearly says \"Portland Bill\".\n\nParenthesised parts are kept in the name: \"Milford (St Ann's)\" (the light is St Ann's Head) and \"Nash (E.)\" (East Nash). You may prefer to split them out.\n\nNo light characters or other columns are printed in this list.",
